second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"When was POSB founded?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0197-7b28e6a7f0f4:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 68, \"text\": \"age of 21 years and full-time National Servicemen from bank charges.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0197-7b28e6a7f0f4:d00\", \"start\": 69, \"end\": 313, \"text\": \"Founded on January 1, 1877 as the \\\"Post Office Savings Bank (POSB)\\\", the bank was part of the Postal Services Department in the Straits Settlements and was set up by the colonial government to provide banking services for lower-income citizens.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0197-7b28e6a7f0f4:d00\", \"start\": 314, \"end\": 549, \"text\": \"Headquartered in the General Post Office Building, in Raffles Place, the bank was under the jurisdiction of the Postmaster-General, with bank policies overseen by a group of trustees appointed by the Governor of the Straits Settlement.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0197-7b28e6a7f0f4:d00\", \"start\": 550, \"end\": 616, \"text\": \"From 1877 to 1940, the bank had a steady growth of accounts opened\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0197-7b28e6a7f0f4:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 72, \"text\": \"mortgages at 12 percent annual interest, with maximum terms of 10 years.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0197-7b28e6a7f0f4:d01\", \"start\": 73, \"end\": 131, \"text\": \"POSB was formed in 1904, as the \\\"Post Office Saving Bank\\\".\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0197-7b28e6a7f0f4:d01\", \"start\": 132, \"end\": 275, \"text\": \"In 1999 the People’s Own Savings Bank Act was established as a corporate body in accordance with the People’s Own Savings Bank of Zimbabwe Act.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0197-7b28e6a7f0f4:d01\", \"start\": 276, \"end\": 570, \"text\": \"In 2001, the Zimbabwe Posts & Telecommunications Corporation (PTC) was split into four independent entities: (a) Net-One, an Internet service provider, (b) Tel-One, a voice communication service provider (land-line and celular) (c) Zimpost, a postal letter carrier and (d) POSB, a savings bank.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0197-7b28e6a7f0f4:d01\", \"start\": 571, \"end\": 621, \"text\": \"The People's Own Savings Bank is 100 percent owned\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0197-7b28e6a7f0f4:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0197-7b28e6a7f0f4:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"POSB\", \"scope\": \"founding date\", \"claim\": \"POSB was founded on January 1, 1877.\", \"answer\": \"January 1, 1877\", \"quote\": \"Founded on January 1, 1877 as the \\\"Post Office Savings Bank (POSB)\\\", the bank was part of the Postal Services Department in the Straits Settlements and was set up by the colonial government to provide banking services for lower-income citizens.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0197-7b28e6a7f0f4:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0197-7b28e6a7f0f4:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"POSB\", \"scope\": \"founding date\", \"claim\": \"POSB was formed in 1904, as the \\\"Post Office Saving Bank\\\".\", \"answer\": \"1904\", \"quote\": \"POSB was formed in 1904, as the \\\"Post Office Saving Bank\\\".\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"R5_answers\": [\"January 1, 1877\", \"1904\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"January 1, 1877\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"1904\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
